#: ../../running/password.rst:2 785d9d835b504c7fa156f0e8f5184a34
msgid "The password, and who can reach this"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/password.rst:4 5ab30656147e4e419a9bf93df9923b6c
msgid ""
"One password for the whole console. Anyone who can reach the page and "
"knows it can create and delete tapes, stop libraries and restart "
"services."
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/password.rst:12 3610fe5793a940e9a56cdca3c9d70551
msgid "The warning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/password.rst:14 569f6752a4ed46a7a435be7100bd1bdb
msgid ""
"While the console still answers to the password it shipped with - "
"``mhvtl`` - every page carries a band saying so:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/password.rst:17 b30473db937e4094b53c611467c98dca
msgid "The default-password warning across the top of a page"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/password.rst:21 e4d02278b3904566a04d946f0add4024
msgid ""
"The **×** on the right puts it away, and that is remembered in your "
"browser. It is a reminder, not a lock: dismissing it changes nothing "
"about the password, and another browser still sees it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/password.rst:26 462b08bb98fd455198d7acab9d80f45f
msgid "Changing it"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/password.rst:28 2ab2689c8b2b45ceb1bcb4f45cf70763
msgid ""
"**Change it now** in the warning, or the **Password** link, at "
"``/auth/password/``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/password.rst:31 acbb16b27b104904ac8bb6123ff3bba0
msgid "The change-password page"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/password.rst:35 e50964582cf14901a7204615481bf3e3
msgid ""
"Three fields - the password you have, the new one twice. On success the "
"console returns to the dashboard, you stay logged in, and the warning is "
"gone from every page, in every browser, because the server stops sending "
"it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/password.rst:39 25f6b07ffc4648cab73c3ff46acb0165
msgid ""
"The old password stops working at once. Logging in with it answers *Wrong"
" Password, Please Try Again*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/password.rst:43 dd7efe84fa5b432eadab61cacbe57dc4
msgid "If you lose it"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/password.rst:45 e01fe10c9bb0433d9a3dafa7afaf62a1
msgid ""
"There is no reset link - there is no email address to send one to. Change"
" it on the server instead:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/password.rst:53 bee6002af7cb49f791931be7a3302a71
msgid "Django asks for the new one twice and writes it to the console's database."
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/password.rst:56 45a60d423a3c4e84a786254b9a61d3a1
msgid "Who can reach the console"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/password.rst:58 42d7e5e2ad23408299e021a4714eaabd
msgid ""
"The password is the only thing between a visitor and every library on "
"this host, so it matters where the console listens:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/password.rst:61 75c80f4407dd4bd5b810ac900b8772da
msgid ""
"The service itself binds ``127.0.0.1:8000`` - not reachable from another "
"machine at all."
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/password.rst:63 dd93628fee444dd587ab7759af4acdef
msgid ""
"nginx serves it on **443** over HTTPS, and redirects **80** to that. On a"
" host where those ports are taken it will be somewhere else - 8443 and "
"8080 are the usual alternative."
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/password.rst:66 6f24226a39944ef3bd71350b9cad28fa
msgid ""
"The certificate the installer creates is self-signed, so a browser asks "
"about it once. Replace ``/etc/pki/tls/certs/mhvtl-gui.crt`` and its key "
"with your own if you have one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/password.rst:70 40f40482f7744ea59b6d9e1f0d06ad76
msgid ""
"``ALLOWED_HOSTS`` in ``/etc/mhvtl-gui/env`` decides which names the "
"console answers to. A request with any other ``Host`` header is refused, "
"which is what stops a machine elsewhere pointing a DNS name at yours."
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/password.rst:75 3040c5d26ca3421988a7711d1aaaca8c
msgid "What the password does not cover"
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/password.rst:77 eae1342a4e7948d191f2cc9dd6900234
msgid ""
"**The command line.** ``mhvtl`` reads the configuration directly and "
"writes through sudo; it has nothing to do with the console's password. "
"Anyone with shell access and the sudo rules can do everything the console"
" can, and more."
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/password.rst:81 dc05d23cf4ad40d0978dbbf7222b8185
msgid ""
"**iSCSI.** An exported library is reachable by anything that can open "
"port 3260, unless the export has an access list or CHAP. Exporting with "
"``--initiator`` limits it to one client; the *iSCSI* guides cover CHAP."
msgstr ""

#: ../../running/password.rst:85 551fff9378854b47a83ed9a40026ac9d
msgid ""
"This console is built for one administrator on a machine they control. It"
" is not multi-user: there are no accounts, no roles, and no audit of who "
"did what."
msgstr ""

